// BT-3580: a block passed to a user-defined higher-order method THROUGH a
// self-send loses both non-local return (^) and captured-local mutation.
// `do:` here is the "self do:" hop every Enumerable-style trait provision
// would need (per BT-3580's own context: found while reviewing the draft
// traits ADR, not yet merged into docs/ADR/) — `detect:ifNone:` and
// `inject:into:` route their caller-supplied block through it via a
// self-send rather than calling `self.items do:` directly, which is the
// exact shape that lost `^` and captured writes before the fix.
//
// See `self_send_hom_sackful.bt` for the Value-class twin (same
// method bodies), which already worked before this fix and pins that it
// keeps working.

Actor subclass: SelfSendHomPool
  state: items = #(1, 2, 3, 4)
  state: total = 0

  // ADR 0128 / BT-3583 regression (review-flagged on PR #4030): a CLASS
  // method forwarding an opaque (non-literal) callable to `collect:`. A
  // class method compiles to `class_<selector>(ClassSelf, ClassVars,
  // Args...)` — it has no `State`/`StateAcc` parameter at all (class-side
  // threading goes through `ClassVars`, not `State`), so the ADR 0128 fold
  // path (which seeds its accumulator from `current_field_read_state_var()`,
  // always `"State"`/`"StateAccN"`) must not run here — it would reference
  // a variable `class_collect:` never binds. Must compile and run
  // correctly, falling back to the pre-ADR plain-value wrapper.
  class classCollect: block => #(1, 2, 3) collect: block

  do: block => self.items do: block

  collect: block => self.items collect: block

  select: block => self.items select: block

  detect: block ifNone: noneBlock =>
    self do: [:each | (block value: each) ifTrue: [^each]]
    noneBlock value

  // `inject:into:` written as `self do: [:each | acc := ...]` (and `size` on
  // top of it) is an ADR 0133 escaping-block compile error since BT-3908: an
  // actor self-send of `do:` is dispatched to this class's own `do:`, so the
  // block escapes (`adr0133_actor_self_send_of_a_collection_message_is_an_escaping_block`).

  // A block that mutates ONLY `self.field`, passed through a self-send to
  // `do:`, is an ADR 0133 compile error since BT-3922 (it raised
  // `stateful_block_dispatch` before). That shape was also the only way to make
  // `do:`'s parameter a promoted Tier 2 position, so `recordAll` below, which
  // BT-3936's case B pinned as a raise, is now the same plain-closure case A as
  // `SelfSendHomPlainPool`.

  // A block that assigns nothing but sends `record:`, which changes a field.
  record: each => self.total := self.total + each

  recordAll =>
    self.total := 0
    self do: [:each | self record: each]
    self.total
